er, without critical chains and regardless of MANUAL/AUTO input mode. One operationId-bound RandomStatsReceipt persists with its original faces; exact replay returns it, a second new roll in the same attempt refuses. Restart/refresh/view never restores a spent right or copies an old version receipt into a new attempt. SENTIENT N+1 preserves its full-sheet workflow with monsterRollContextOrNull=null and no ENM-018/019 action; forged monster context refuses. Error/offline: Для ENM-011, ENM-012, ENM-013, ENM-014, ENM-015, ENM-016, ENM-018, ENM-019 проверить invalid field/failed guard, stale revision, disconnect before commit, disconnect after commit-before-ack и idempotent replay: до commit — zero write, после commit — прежний receipt без повторного эффекта. | Terminal states/deltas: {"audit": "Every committed mutation records author/target/timestamp/before/after/reason/source and resulting revision.", "mutationBoundary": "Only listed executableOperationIds/workflowCommandIds may write; all other routes are navigation/read-only.", "terminalStatesByForm": {"ENM-011": ["DRAFTING", "STAGE_VALID"], "ENM-012": ["MANUAL_EDIT", "ROLL_NOT_USED", "ROLL_COMMITTED", "STAGE_VALID"], "ENM-013": ["INVALID_PHYSICS", "STAGE_VALID"], "ENM-014": ["INVALID_ATTACK", "STAGE_VALID"], "ENM-015": ["INVALID_SYMBIONT", "STAGE_VALID"], "ENM-016": ["BLOCKED_INVALID", "READY_TO_COMMIT", "COMMITTED"], "ENM-018": ["NOT_ROLLED", "ROLLING", "COMMITTED"]}} Reconnect assertions: Uncommitted local input may restore as draft but never as confirmed state.; Committed command restores by commandId with the same receipt/random result and no duplicate side effect.; Fresh server projection recomputes allowed CTA/targets and omits stale or forbidden actions from payload/DOM/a11y/hotkeys/cache. Owner decision #186 D: a host-bound CUSTOM_MONSTER technical attempt carries attemptId, attemptRevision, campaignId and originFormId=ENM-012\|ENM-017. Existing monsterDraftId/creationAttemptId are exact aliases of that same attemptId, never separate identities. Creation binds origin ENM-012; version editing binds origin ENM-017 plus templateId and expectedCurrentVersion. The host, never a free client returnFormId, chooses every child return. SENTIENT, system templates and foreign/stale attempts cannot enter this channel. On ENM-017 monsterRollContextOrNull is null for SENTIENT and the closed bound context for CUSTOM_MONSTER; null never grants a roll or receipt CTA. CORE-201: each distinct creation or version attempt has its own single roll right. The host produces exactly seven independent natural R20 in S,D,M,Z,I,W,C order, without critical chains and regardless of MANUAL/AUTO input mode. One operationId-bound RandomStatsReceipt persists with its original faces; exact replay returns it, a second new roll in the same attempt refuses. Restart/refresh/view never restores a spent right or copies an old version receipt into a new attempt. Returning from ENM-018/019 restores the same confirmed attempt and receipt, including after a roll; it never rerolls, rolls back randomness or overwrites later manual candidate edits. Only the receipt/original roll is immutable; candidate base stats remain manually editable within CORE-200 1..35. Canceling version editing preserves the prior currentVersion and does not erase its attempt receipt. |
